## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates end-to-end KCA design skills for on-premises edge deployments, multi-tenant isolation, offline resilience, and firmware OTA in a distributed partner network.

## Key Concepts
- Hardware root of trust and regional bootstrap services
- Per-tenant trust anchors with SPIFFE-based identity assignment
- Offline and partial connectivity resilience with robust revocation mechanisms
- Post-quantum cryptography (PQC) agility for future-proofing
- OTA firmware signing and secure update workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
function buildCSR(tenant, rackId, spiffeId) {
  return {
    commonName: rackId,
    organization: tenant,
    subjectAltName: {
      type: 'spiffe',
      value: spiffeId
    },
    keyUsage: ['digitalSignature', 'keyEncipherment'],
    extKeyUsage: ['serverAuth', 'clientAuth']
  };
}

async function bootstrapRack(config, regionalService) {
  const attestation = await config.platform.quote();
  const response = await regionalService.attest(attestation);

  if (response.status === 'approved') {
    return enrollWithKCA(response.enrollmentToken, config);
  }
  throw new Error('Attestation failed');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Interview to test token-based enrollment, per-tenant policy, and practical gateway validation with renewal and failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- Token-based enrollment (JWT)
- Short-lived client certificates (2h)
- Gateway tenant mapping and cert validation
- Renewal and revocation strategies
- Clock skew handling and audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
function isCertValid(cert, now=new Date()) {
  const nb = new Date(cert.notBefore).getTime();
  const na = new Date(cert.notAfter).getTime();
  const skew = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 minutes
  if (now.getTime() < nb - skew) return false;
  if (now.getTime() > na + skew) return false;
  if (cert.subject?.CN !== cert.tenantId) return false;
  return true;
}
```

